From e8afd91bd67867d6ea20614927463118675612c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenTTD P0 Instrumentation <p0-instrumentation@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:58:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] port003: add fail-closed trace sink foundation

Add the opt-in Linux-only OPTION_P0_ORACLE_TRACE build boundary and a checked little-endian sink that writes exclusively to a .partial journal, retains failures, and durably closes output for the independent C17 finalizer.

The patch anchors at set_options/add_definitions_based_on_options and the src add_files lists. It does not sample gameplay state or enter a command/tick boundary; later patches own those integration points.
